2.give me pql for pod monitoring
1️⃣ CPU Usage per Pod
sum(rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{namespace="default", pod=~".+"}[5m])) by (pod)


Explanation:

container_cpu_usage_seconds_total → cumulative CPU time for container

rate(...[5m]) → CPU usage per second over last 5 minutes

sum by (pod) → sum across all containers in the pod

Use case: Grafana panel for CPU utilization per pod.

2️⃣ Memory Usage per Pod
sum(container_memory_usage_bytes{namespace="default", pod=~".+"}) by (pod)


Explanation:

Shows memory used by all containers in a pod

Use container_memory_working_set_bytes to exclude cache/buffers

3️⃣ Pod Restarts (Critical Alert)
increase(kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total{namespace="default"}[10m]) > 0


Explanation:

kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total → total restarts per container

increase(...[10m]) > 0 → pod restarted in last 10 minutes

Can trigger alert if pod is unstable

4️⃣ Pods Not Ready
kube_pod_status_ready{condition="false", namespace="default"} == 1


Explanation:

Checks pods with Ready=false

Trigger alert if pod remains unready for for: 5m

5️⃣ Pod CPU Saturation (%)
100 * sum(rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{namespace="default", pod=~".+"}[5m]))
   / sum(kube_pod_container_resource_limits_cpu_cores{namespace="default", pod=~".+"}) by (pod)


Explanation:

Calculates CPU usage as percentage of pod CPU limit

Great for SRE dashboards / alerts

6️⃣ Pod Memory Saturation (%)
100 * sum(container_memory_usage_bytes{namespace="default", pod=~".+"})
   / sum(kube_pod_container_resource_limits_memory_bytes{namespace="default", pod=~".+"}) by (pod)


Explanation:

Memory usage as % of requested limit

Avoids alerting on pods under heavy buffer/cache memory

7️⃣ Network Traffic per Pod
sum(rate(container_network_receive_bytes_total{namespace="default", pod=~".+"}[5m])) by (pod)


Same for transmit: container_network_transmit_bytes_total

Use case: Track bandwidth per pod / detect traffic spikes

8️⃣ Disk Usage per Pod (if ephemeral storage used)
sum(container_fs_usage_bytes{namespace="default", pod=~".+"}) by (pod)


Use case: Alert if pods are filling ephemeral storage

9️⃣ Pod Count per Namespace
count(kube_pod_info{namespace="default"}) by (namespace)


Use case: Monitor expected number of pods per namespace

10️⃣ Pod CrashLoopBackOff Detection
kube_pod_container_status_waiting_reason{reason="CrashLoopBackOff", namespace="default"}


Use case: Alert if any pod enters CrashLoopBackOff
Mention namespace filtering: namespace="default" or dynamic with Grafana variable $n
